# SLP — work partitioning in this repo

**Prerequisite:** `core.law-gate.mdc` (`AGENTS.md` has been **Read**). This rule does **not** replace `AGENTS.md`; it is the
work-partitioning mechanism when a request needs more than one edit round. Runtime skill: `harness-engineering-team`
(`agents/skills/`). Workers: `agents/subagents/*-runtime.md` (**7**) — each host receives the **generated** copy under
`<tree>/agents/` (`.cursor/` · `.agents/`); never edit generated copies by hand.

> Source: measured on **baplatform** (`.cursor/agents/`, 7 roles) — `sdlc/07.technical/01.architecture/16.jira-ticket-contract.md` §10
> and `17.jira-slp-operating.md`. What is kept and what changes for ESO is recorded in §8 of `17`; this rule is the executable form.

## 0. Operator shorthand

```text
impl <KEY> slp g
```

| Token | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `impl` | implement the ticket identified by `<KEY>` |
| `slp` | run SLP: scout → plan → build → verify → audit → Human In Review |
| `g` | gate + guardrails: scope · status · contract · evidence (§4.1) |

The shorthand is deliberately small. It MUST resolve to this rule; guardrails MUST NOT be re-typed into every prompt.

## 1. Four layers — who may do what

| Layer | Who | Gates |
|---|---|---|
| **S** Supervisor | **human** (operator), **outside** the loop | approve plan for large/ambiguous scope · handle escalation · **sign `Done`** |
| **L** Lead | main chat agent | read pack · split slices · spawn workers · write `Human In Review` · roll up |
| **P** Peer | `scout` · `plan` · `build` (one slice at a time) · `fixbug` | no crosstalk; `allowed_files` are **disjoint** |
| **A** Gate | `verify` (deterministic) · `audit` (rubric) · `qc` (scenario) | independent of builder; **must not** edit `agents/` · `scripts/` · `tools/` |

**S is never an agent.** An agent that signs its own `Done` is a fake process.

## 2. Seven workers — pairwise-disjoint `allowed_files`

| Worker | `allowed_files` (write) | Reads | Returns |
|---|---|---|---|
| `scout` | `/tmp/slp/recon/` | `agents/`, `scripts/`, `sdlc/01.agent-manifests/01.domains/` | `domains[]` · `inv[]` · `touched_files[]` · `open_gaps[]` · `risks[]` (**≤300 words, no code**) |
| `plan` | `/tmp/slp/plan/` | domain spec · `sdlc/09.wbs/` | `slices[]`: `id` · `role` · `ac[]` · `inv[]` · `allowed_files[]` · `depends_on[]` · `verify` |
| `build` | `agents/` (**source** — not `.cursor/**`/`.agents/**`) · `scripts/` · `tools/` | slice + AC rows | `slice` · `status` `DONE\|BLOCKED_SCOPE` · `files_changed[]` · `tests_added[]` |
| `fixbug` | **derived** — `findings[].file`, subset of the FAIL slice | audit JSON / failure log | `status` · `root_cause` · `fix[]` |
| `verify` | `/tmp/slp/verify/` | Task verify command | `status` PASS/FAIL · `commands_run[]` · `failure_log` |
| `audit` | `/tmp/slp/audit/` | `git diff` · INV · AC | `verdict` · `score` · `critical[]` · `findings[{file,line,rule,fix}]` · `ac_coverage{}` |
| `qc` | `/tmp/slp/qc/` | scenario matrix · `sdlc/` | `status` · `failed_gates[]` · `scenarios_run[]` · `residual_open[]` |

**Law:** the intersection of **any two** `allowed_files` sets is ∅. The Lead checks every pair before assigning slices; `audit`
re-checks in `findings[]`. `fixbug` has no static set: it may write only files named by `audit.findings[].file` or the failure log,
and those files must belong to the failing slice. Anything else ⇒ `BLOCKED_SCOPE`; stop and report to the Lead.

**Why `build` owns `agents/` + `scripts/` + `tools/`, while `qc` only reads:** `agents/` is the **single source** of agent
configuration (`D-108`). Editing `.cursor/**` or `.agents/**` edits a **generated artifact**; drift is blocked by
`build-host-trees.mjs --check`. `qc` runs scenarios and writes its own evidence: a builder that writes scenarios and grades
itself is **grading its own work**.

**Why gates write only to `/tmp/slp/`:** gates return JSON and the Lead assembles it. `/tmp/slp/` is per-session evidence, not
documentation, so gates do not create a **second source of truth** (§A1).

## 3. Prompt contract — always four parts

`INV ids` · `AC rows in scope` · `allowed_files` · `verify command`.

If one part is missing, the worker **asks again**; it **does not guess**. `plan` emits exactly four parts per slice; the Lead
forwards them verbatim.

## 4. Hard rules

1. **Blackboard DAG** — workers talk only to the Lead. No worker-to-worker, no group chat.
2. **Disjoint slices** — overlapping `allowed_files` is an invalid plan; split again. Writing outside the slice ⇒ `BLOCKED_SCOPE`.
3. **Zero-crawl** — peers receive the pack in the prompt; they **must not** read `sdlc/01…09` to rebuild context.
4. **Gate order** — build → verify PASS → `AUDIT_PASS` (**≥85**, **0 CRITICAL**) → `Human In Review`. QC **only** when the operator asks.
5. **Loop cap** — the same root error **3** times ⇒ stop, list `OPEN`, escalate **to S** (not to another agent).
6. **No self-grading** — `verify`/`audit`/`qc` do not edit code; `build`/`fixbug` do not declare the final PASS.
7. **No `Done`, no commit/push/PR** unless S asks. Do not move another person's ticket to `In Progress`. After every child
   transition, roll up the parent: child `In Progress` ⇒ parent `In Progress`; all children `Human In Review`/`Done` ⇒ parent
   `Human In Review`; never auto-`Done` (rule: `delivery.jira-agent-execution`).
8. **Small tickets** — the Lead may work **inline** (no spawn) but **still** runs verify **and** audit.
9. **Honesty when tools are missing** — no codegraph/docgraph ⇒ say so and fall back to `grep`/`read`; MCP Brain down ⇒
   `BRAIN_UNAVAILABLE`, stop. **Never** claim success.

### 4.1 Guardrails (`g`)

These apply to every `impl … slp g` run. They do not replace audit; they constrain the builder before audit.

| id | Guardrail | Required behavior |
|---|---|---|
| **G1** | **Scope** | Write only inside the ticket/packet `allowed_files`. If a required file is outside, STOP with `BLOCKED_SCOPE` and name the file/contract to be authorized. Never expand scope silently. |
| **G2** | **Status** | Before code: move the ticket and its subtasks to `In Progress`. On PASS: move the ticket and its subtasks to `Human In Review`. On FAIL: keep them `In Progress`, add label `blocked`, and comment the failure. Never `Done`/`Closed`. |
| **G3** | **Contract** | Do not change AC, error codes, schema, or API contract silently. If the contract is missing or contradictory, STOP and report the exact conflict. Do not invent contracts or tables. |
| **G4** | **Evidence** | Report files changed, exact commands run, real results, out-of-scope files, and residual gaps. No commit/push. A green claim without a command log is invalid. |

Guardrail failures are `BLOCKED_SCOPE` or `BLOCKED_CONTRACT`, never a silent PASS.

## 5. Gates — numbered

| # | Gate | Input | Output |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Intake** | request | `class`: `agent-config` (`agents/`, `scripts/`) · `law/spec` (`sdlc/`) · `ticket` |
| 2 | **Pack** | ticket/key | ticket + domain spec + AC + verify command (if incomplete ⇒ spawn `scout`; do not guess) |
| 3 | **Session** | — | law Read · MCP/brain per `core.harness-tooling.mdc` |
| 4 | **Plan** — **S-GATE 1** when >1 layer or ambiguous scope | pack | slice table, disjoint `allowed_files`, every AC mapped to exactly **one** slice |
| 5 | **Build × N** | slice | `DONE` or `BLOCKED_SCOPE`; parallel when `depends_on` is empty |
| 6 | **Verify** | built slice | PASS/FAIL + verbatim log; FAIL ⇒ `fixbug` ↺ |
| 7 | **Audit** | verify PASS | rubric §6; FAIL ⇒ `fixbug` ↺; **3** rounds ⇒ **S-GATE 2** |
| 8 | **Human In Review** | AUDIT_PASS | comment + label + rollup. **No** `Done` |
| 9 | **QC** | operator request | matrix PASS/FAIL/BLOCKED — **S-GATE 3**: human signs `Done` |

## 6. `audit` rubric — four criteria

| Points | Criterion | Measured by |
|---:|---|---|
| 30 | **Deterministic green** | `verify` PASS **in this session**: `node scripts/build-host-trees.mjs --check` **and** `node scripts/check-dual-harness.mjs` green |
| 30 | **Invariants** | no **second source of truth**: edit only `agents/`, not provider trees (`.cursor/**`, `.agents/**`) · do not change thresholds in code · do not replace `unknown` by default · `D-108` rules 1–7 |
| 25 | **AC complete, no invented contract** | every AC in scope is proven; new fields/paths are cited from `AGENTS.md`, a rule in `agents/rules/`, or `sdlc/` — never from memory |
| 15 | **Boundary discipline** | edit only the slice `allowed_files`; gates do not write `agents/` |

**CRITICAL** (INV violation · **second source of truth** · invented API · **fake green**) ⇒ criterion 2 = **0**, verdict **FAIL**
regardless of total score. A CRITICAL finding must not be averaged away by high scores elsewhere.

## 7. Verify commands by layer — **dev, not operator**

| Touch | Command |
|---|---|
| `agents/rules/`, `agents/subagents/`, `agents/skills/` | **Lead**: `node scripts/build-host-trees.mjs` then `--check` · `node scripts/check-dual-harness.mjs` (workers do not write trees) |
| `agents/hooks/`, `agents/instructions.md` | same as above (same generator) |
| `scripts/` | `node <script> --check` if present; this repo has no separate test runner for scripts |
| any change | **effective only after** the generator runs — provider trees are artifacts, not source |

Verify commands **come from** `agents/rules/` and the repo gate scripts; do not invent them. A task without a verify command ⇒
`FAIL`, `MISSING_VERIFY_PLAN`. Product code packages may define their own test commands in their packets; the repo-level gates
still apply.

## 8. Evidence — six items

`class` · pack read · codegraph/docgraph **status** · verify commands + log · `audit` **score/verdict** · slice + files written.
Missing evidence ⇒ **do not** say "done". See also `core.harness-agents.mdc` and `harness-engineering-team`.

## 9. Three things **not** copied from BAP

| BAP | ESO | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `[be]` `[fe]` `[mo]` `[qc]` | **drop `[mo]`**; keep `[be]` `[fe]` `[qc]` | no mobile |
| QC only after UT/COV/DEV `Done` (G-QC-06/07/08) | **QC runs when the operator asks** (`D-41`) | one human: waiting for `Done` is waiting for yourself |
| `dotnet build/test/format` | `node scripts/build-host-trees.mjs --check` · `node scripts/check-dual-harness.mjs` | different stack |

**Kept:** quartet `tdd-unit`/`tdd-impl`/`tdd-coverage`/`tdd-qc` · link graph `Blocks`/`Relates` · purposes P-01…P-07 ·
anti-patterns J-01…J-17 · atomic WBS "one subtask = one file or one command".

## 10. `READY` is **plan-ready**, not **tested** — `D-81`

Hard order, never reversed:

```text
BA AC → QC writes SCN (sdlc/06.analysis/03.scn, status `planned`)
      → packet §7 AC → SCN → RED/GREEN → §9 READY
      → tdd-unit (RED) → tdd-impl (GREEN) → tdd-coverage → tdd-qc RUN SCN + RTM
```

A packet `READY` that requires "SCN already run" reverses the order and locks itself. Plane `E` records only
`OK` / `OK — partial` / `OPEN` / `OUT`, never run progress. This repo's product packages may have their own test runner;
the repo itself does not: verify by review + `audit`. Decision: `sdlc/03.inception/02-decision-log/06.architecture-va-data.md` `D-81`.

## 11. Multi-provider binding (DSH Lead & Gate, AGY Peer)

When splitting roles between **DeepSeek Harness (DSH)** and **Antigravity (AGY)**:
1. **DSH is Lead & Gate**:
   - **Lead (L):** analyze, run `plan-runtime` to split independent slices, control S-GATE 1 (operator approves plan).
   - **Gate & QC (A):** run deterministic verify (`build-host-trees.mjs --check` + `check-dual-harness.mjs`), run
     `audit-runtime` against the rubric (≥85, 0 CRITICAL), and run `qc-runtime` when requested.
2. **AGY is Peer (P)**:
   - DSH **does not** edit `agents/` while acting as gate.
   - For each approved slice, DSH invokes AGY CLI:
     ```bash
     agy -p "<4-part prompt: INV, AC, allowed_files, verify command>" \
       --agent build-runtime \
       --dangerously-skip-permissions \
       --output-format json
     ```
   - AGY receives the 4-part contract and edits only that slice's `allowed_files`.
3. **SLP invariant:** builder (AGY) and gate (DSH) are independent; a builder never grades its own code.
